  "title": "The Returning Picnic Table",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A block family needs a picnic table on a bare square, but every piece is stored beneath a different paving tile. Opening the first compartment raises a leg that unlocks the next compartment; the final tabletop rotates into place, and the now-empty compartments become matching seats.",
  "hook": "The park is hiding our lunch furniture.",
  "visible_action": "Ground tiles flip; legs rise and latch; a tabletop rotates; remaining cavities lift seat blocks to ground level.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A deployment sequence can give emptied spaces a second purpose.",
  "gate": "Clearly a toy world; no safe real furniture specification is implied.",
